From 6e87684b52f59d1fb45cfa47d4115845a20bdaad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ccr <ccr@aciceri.dev>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 13:03:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] collab-client: re-vendor with remote live voice and interface
 scale

Re-vendors packages/collab-web from oh-my-pi v18.1.15 plus the remote
live-voice series, merged three-way against the previous pin so every local
gateway patch is preserved: in-memory capability bootstrap, embedded mode,
browser connection recovery, markdown link scheme validation, transcript
windowing, photo action.

collab-web is byte-identical between v18.1.14 and v18.1.15, so the previous
pin is an exact merge base.

The pinned @oh-my-pi/pi-wire 18.1.14 predates the live frames and a union
cannot be extended by declaration merging, so lib/live-frames.ts declares
the four host frames and two guest frames the client consumes and narrows
them before the pinned union switch. GatewayGuestFrame gains them the same
way it already gains gateway-health-ping.

Embedded gateway mode suppresses the client header, which is where the
microphone control lives, so LivePanel takes an optional onStart and becomes
the sole entry point there instead of duplicating a header button.
